{
  "id": "Compound::DB00331 - Gene::91942",
  "verbalization": "Metformin is shown to interact with Ndufa8, Ndufa7, and Ndufs7, all of which are subunits of the Nadh dehydrogenase (ubiquinone) complex. These subunits are involved in the activity of the complex, which is ultimately participated by Ndufaf2. The evidence suggests that Metformin may influence the activity of this complex through binding to one of its subunits, potentially altering the overall function of the Nadh dehydrogenase complex. This mechanism implies that Metformin could modulate Ndufaf2's role in the complex, possibly through indirect effects on the complex's activity. The consistent involvement of these subunits in the same functional pathway supports the idea that Metformin's interaction with Ndufa8, Ndufa7, or Ndufs7 may lead to a broader impact on Ndufaf2's function, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
